+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
                        MINI QUEST COMMANDS
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

  There are various commands that you'll need when doing quests:

  * "qlist"       This command lists all available quests. All quests
                  are color coded by difficult based on level guidelines
                  of the quest, and your current level. You can filter
                  by domain, level, deity, reputation, type, tag, or
                  status. Examples: "qlist deity set", "qlist rep
                  villain", "qlist level 1-10".

  * "qinfo [#]"   This command prints out details for the given quest 
                  using the number shown in your most recent "qlist".

  * "myquests"    This command lists all quests that you have accepted.
                  To accept a quest, you would use the "qaccept" command.

  * "qaccept [#]" As previously mentioned, you use the qaccept command
                  and the quest number found in your most recent
                  "qlist".

  * "qactive [#]" This command is kept for compatibility. Active quests
                  are no longer required.

  * "qstatus"     This gives you an at a glance status of your accepted
                  unfinished quests.

  * "escort"      If one of your accepted quests has an escort objective,
                  and the mob does not automatically begin his journey
                  you use this command to begin the escort of the 
                  target mob.

